{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310758,"nonce":"KZLAiFWBWwd8H74m68imsckGEm4=","title":"2026-09-24 nightly Windows fixes — new runtime exports MUST be register_symbol!'d (Windows has no dlsym fallback); parser spans index ...","message":"Nightly windows-x86_64 failed 09-21..09-24 (fixed be849899, f6eacd09; issue 75fbed89). JIT flake fixed 05dd5a81 (issue d371a06c).\n\n- **Every new `#[no_mangle]` runtime export needs `register_symbol!` in runtime/src/plugin_impl.rs.** macOS/Linux silently fall back to the process symbol table; Windows does not, so a missing entry only surfaces as `can't resolve symbol X` in the Windows nightly. Guard: `cargo test -p rayzor-runtime --lib every_export_is_registered` (HOST_ONLY allowlist for exports the compiler never names).\n- **Parser spans index the PREPROCESSED source**, not the file: `lines()` drops `\\r` (CRLF shifts a byte per line) and `#if` branches are replaced by blank lines. Never slice raw source by a span. Metadata now carries `compile_time` (`@:`) from the token. The old slice also broke LF input after `#if` (haxe.macro.Context `@allow`), which is why TestRest moved CRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER.\n- Reproduce a Windows CRLF issue on the Mac: `perl -pi -e 's/\\n/\\r\\n/'` the stdlib file (compiler/haxe-std), run, `git checkout` it.\n- x86-64 Cranelift JIT: calls between a module's functions are PCRel4 with no fallback; `codegen/jit_memory.rs` carves allocations from one ArenaMemoryProvider (1GB, 64MB on Windows) and falls back to system mappings when full.\n- nuc: use `~/nuc-ci.sh \u003ccmd\u003e` (stable toolchain + LLVM 21 env, tree synced to ~/rayzor-ci); the default nightly toolchain there fails to link compiler tests. Clippy there: `~/.cargo/bin/cargo clippy` WITHOUT the RUSTC override. The Mac cannot lint x86-only cfg code.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_use_nuc_not_local_vms_for_linux]], [[feedback_moved_rows_are_where_regressions_hide]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_windows_nightly_symbols_crlf_jit_reach` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}